BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 5: Use Windows
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T113000
UID:69d93d43f29b90618efdf8e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on essential basic Windows skills for absolute beginne
 rs with little computer experience.\nIn this fifth session you will:\nBeco
 me familiar with the Windows (10) operating system\nPractice using common 
 Windows features: File Explorer\, Desktop\, Taskbar\, Windows\, Applicatio
 ns\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic understanding
  of how to create and organize files in the Windows environment.\nPrerequi
 sites: Computer for Beginners 1 & 2 or basic mouse and keyboarding skills\
 nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-
 5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Kennedy/Eglinton\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d93d43f29b90618efdf8e9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Evening Book Club & Play Reading
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T200000
UID:6972a805d2bbe265eb294671@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join other book lovers in your community and participate in li
 vely discussions of popular books.\nMeeting every 1\nst\nTuesday of the mo
 nth. We will be discussing the following\nJune 2\,\n2026\n– Looking for 
 Jane by Heather Marshall\nWe will be selecting book club titles for the f
 ollowing year.\nCopies of the book are available for borrowing at the Fair
 view Library.\nAll are welcome. Drop-in\, no registration necessary.
LOCATION:Fairview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6972a805d2bbe265eb294671
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Movies 
 Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T163000
UID:6931f2a276261f28005d7d58@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come and join the F.R.E.S.H. group for a Saturday screening of popular mov
 ies.\nWe'll be playing the following films\nMay 30\nth\n– Green Book\nJu
 ne 6\nth\n– A River Runs Through It\nJune 13\nth\n– Planes\, Trains an
 d Automobiles\nJune 20\nth\n– The Grapes of Wrath (1940)\nJune 27\nth\n
 –\nWalk the Line\nDrop in\, no registration is required.\nSnacks and ref
 reshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be avai
 lable at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Cri
 sis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, First floor\, Activity Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f2a276261f28005d7d58
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
